{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 118, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With no 1->3 edge the output lacks a strong path, so adding a 0->3 conv gives more gain than when edge 4 already provides one."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip to the output adds more when edge 4 is absent and few other paths reach node 3."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A strong conv on edge 0 feeds the 0->1->2 chain so a conv on edge 2 uses real features."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 2 discards a path that is valuable only when edge 0 is a strong conv, so the drop is larger."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Edge 0 feeds the 0->1->2 chain, so a conv there pays off more when edge 2 is a conv than when it is none."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with nothing loses more than replacing a skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a strong conv hurts more than deleting a weak op like skip."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a conv edge costs more than removing a skip connection."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the input conv edge costs more than removing a skip, since edge 0 feeds all downstream paths."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_